// the generated views.
//
// FORMAT: a zero-dependency ES data module (not YAML) - the repo's scripts are
// strictly zero-dep and Node has no built-in YAML parser. A .mjs object literal keeps
// the YAML ergonomics the spec wanted (inline comments, multi-line reasoning, no
// quote-escaping, trailing commas, diff-friendly) while staying parser-free: every
// consumer (gen-registry.mjs, check-registry.mjs, the Astro site) is Node and imports
// it directly. The contract is frameworks/registry.schema.json; scripts/check-registry.mjs
// enforces it. This file must contain ONLY data (an exported object literal), no logic.
//
// FAMILY NOTE: `family` uses the 13-family CATALOG (universe) taxonomy, which differs
// by design from the live skill metadata.family slugs (a separate, coarser grouping the
// 47 shipped skills + the Astro families/ pages use). The registry must cover all 135
// methods, most of which are unbuilt and have no skill metadata; harmonizing the two
// taxonomies is a noted follow-up, out of scope for SP3.
//
