      reasoning: "Re-vetted 2026-06-09 (think-research-framework): [cand/build/C] -> [fold]. Dialectical synthesis is a stance (set a position against its opposite, then reconcile), not a procedure with its own artifact, and each concrete thing it produces is already owned. The reproducible solo-agent version - state the thesis, build its strongest antithesis, then reconcile - is mechanically red-team-light (construct the strongest opposing case, then judge which objections land and what would rebut them, which is the synthesis tail in miniature); the shared machinery is well above the ~20% ceiling and dialectical synthesis adds only the name of the third step. The evidenced version - dialectical inquiry's plan-vs-counter-plan debate to surface assumptions (Mason 1969; Mason and Mitroff 1981; Schweiger, Sandberg and Ragan 1986) - is a structured-conflict group technique whose validated core already ships as authentic-dissent (Nemeth's role-played-dissent-fails result is load-bearing in both), with authentic-dissent itself routing constructed opposition to red-team-light. The integrate-to-a-better-third tail is contradiction-resolution (dissolve the trade-off) or contradiction-tension-mapping (hold the polarity); the numeric average-two-opposed-estimates version is dialectical bootstrapping (Herzog and Hertwig 2009), a separate estimation trick. Evidence governed at C: the synthesis-production move has no direct controlled evidence; Schwenk's 1990 meta-analysis finds dialectical inquiry's edge over devil's advocacy not robust and DI no better than the expert approach on ill-structured tasks, so the experimental robustness in the neighborhood belongs to structured conflict and numeric averaging, both explicitly not counted toward this entry (grading up would launder a cousin's robustness onto the synthesis step). Transferred from human subjects, not agent-validated. Fold into red-team-light as the construct-opposition-then-reconcile home. Generic philosophical/management term, attributed to the Fichte/Hegel lineage and the Mason/Mitroff program, not branded. Wave-3 note (2026-06-11): dialectical bootstrapping, which this reasoning already treats as a separate estimation trick whose robustness was explicitly not counted here, is unbundled from this entry's aliases into its own candidate row.",
